1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:07,610
DIMNA: Kalila, you would never trust a hungry heron, right? But 10 little fish did, and they almost lost their home!

2
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:10,780
KALILA: Ten little fish? Oh no! Who saved them?

3
00:00:10,930 --> 00:00:14,590
DIMNA: Someone very small, with two very strong claws. Listen!

4
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:26,310
Once upon a time, by a sparkling blue lake, there lived an old heron. Every day, he caught fish for his dinner.

5
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:30,690
But now he was old and slow, and the fish swam away too fast.

6
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:36,830
HERON: Oh, my legs are tired, and my beak is slow. How will I get my dinner?

7
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:41,120
HERON: Hmm... If I cannot catch them, I will trick them!

8
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:48,540
So the heron stood by the water, looking very, very sad. A little crab saw him from her rock.

9
00:00:48,990 --> 00:00:51,320
CRAB: Uncle Heron, why are you so sad today?

10
00:00:51,770 --> 00:01:00,250
HERON: Oh, little crab! I heard the fishermen talking. Tomorrow they will come with big nets, and take all the fish away!

11
00:01:00,650 --> 00:01:02,110
FISH: Oh no! What can we do?

12
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:04,000
LITTLE FISH: Please help us, Uncle Heron!

13
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:12,760
HERON: Don't worry, my dears. Behind the big rocks, there is a beautiful new lake. I will carry you there, one by one.

14
00:01:13,310 --> 00:01:15,430
The fish believed his sweet words.

15
00:01:17,030 --> 00:01:26,470
So every day, the heron carried a fish away in his beak. But there was no beautiful lake. He dropped them into a tiny muddy puddle, behind the rocks.

16
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:31,920
HERON: Hee hee! My little dinner pond. I will eat you all, one by one!

17
00:01:32,370 --> 00:01:34,090
LITTLE FISH: Help! This is not a beautiful lake!

18
00:01:35,490 --> 00:01:38,340
CRAB: Uncle Heron, take me too! I want to see the new lake.

19
00:01:38,790 --> 00:01:43,850
HERON: A crab? Hmm, crab for dinner... Yes, yes! Climb up on my neck!

20
00:01:45,850 --> 00:01:52,710
Up, up they flew, over the big rocks. The crab looked down, and she saw the tiny puddle, full of scared fish!

21
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:55,130
CRAB: That is not a lake! You tricked us!

22
00:01:55,330 --> 00:01:59,970
So the clever crab held on to the heron's neck with her claws, and... pinch!

23
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:02,500
HERON: Ow! Ow! Let me go!

24
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:05,740
CRAB: First, put me down. And never trick the fish again!

25
00:02:06,190 --> 00:02:09,950
HERON: Ow! All right, all right! I'm sorry! I'm going!

26
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:15,410
The heron put the crab down, and flew far, far away. And he never came back.

27
00:02:16,810 --> 00:02:24,110
Then the crab dug a little stream with her claws, from the puddle, all the way back to the lake. And all the fish swam home!

28
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:26,340
FISH: Hooray! Thank you, clever crab!

29
00:02:26,790 --> 00:02:30,130
CRAB: Remember, friends: sweet words are not always true words!

30
00:02:32,330 --> 00:02:38,570
KALILA: So the heron said sweet words, but they were lies. Only the crab looked with her own eyes.

31
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:41,370
DIMNA: Don't believe sweet lies! Look and check first!

32
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:46,660
DIMNA: Persian word of the day! In Persian, a fish is maahi. Maahi! Blub, blub!

33
00:02:46,810 --> 00:02:51,110
KALILA: Maahi. A fish. And our little maahi are safe at home now.

34
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:58,090
KALILA: And next time: a tortoise who wants to fly, and two kind ducks with a stick.

